hyphens: a-b-c
colon: hello:world
command: sudo apt-get install foo
user: 1000:984
volumes:
  - ./html:/var/www/html
  - a-b
json: {"a":1, "b":[2]}

----------------------------------------------------

[
	["key", "hyphens"],
	["punctuation", ":"],
	" a-b-c\r\n",

	["key", "colon"],
	["punctuation", ":"],
	" hello:world\r\n",

	["key", "command"],
	["punctuation", ":"],
	" sudo apt-get install foo\r\n",

	["key", "user"],
	["punctuation", ":"],
	" 1000:984\r\n",

	["key", "volumes"],
	["punctuation", ":"],

	["punctuation", "-"],
	" ./html:/var/www/html\r\n  ",

	["punctuation", "-"],
	" a-b\r\n",

	["key", "json"],
	["punctuation", ":"],
	["punctuation", "{"],
	"\"a\"",
	["punctuation", ":"],
	["number", "1"],
	["punctuation", ","],
	" \"b\"",
	["punctuation", ":"],
	["punctuation", "["],
	["number", "2"],
	["punctuation", "]"],
	["punctuation", "}"]
]

----------------------------------------------------

Checks that `-` and `:` inside plain scalars are not highlighted as punctuation, while `-` and `:`
followed by a space or directly following a quoted key still are.

See https://github.com/PrismJS/prism/issues/2563 and https://github.com/PrismJS/prism/issues/3586
